title: Education & Science
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: spd_in_government and chancellor_party = "SPD" and education_science_timer = 0
on-arrival: education_science_timer += 9; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/portraits/EinsteinAlbert.jpg
go-to: ed_menu
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

# science increases economic growth...

= Education and Science

Education in Germany is the responsibility of the state governments. With our control over many states, we can 

[? if major_curriculum: Current educational curriculum - [+ major_curriculum +], [+ minor_curriculum +] ?]

@ed_menu
view-if: not last_advisor_action

- @increase_science
- @structure
- @curriculum
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action


@increase_science
title: Increase funding for scientific research.
choose-if: economic_minister_party = "SPD"
unavailable-subtitle: This requires the Economic Ministry.

Socialism has always stood for science and rationality. Despite the setbacks of the two world wars, economic crises, and the politicized and reactionary attitudes of many academics, science in the German Republic is still the envy of the world. With a great expansion of funding, we hope to keep it that way, and expand on our achievements. 

- @mpg
- @applied
- @medical
- @cut_funding
- @ed_menu: Do not increase research funding.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@mpg
title: Fund the Max Planck Society for basic scientific research.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; science += 1; mpg_research += 1; economic_growth += 0.3 if economic_growth <= 8; white_collar_workers_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent); fdp_relation += 5*(1-dissent); science_funding += 1

The Max Planck Society, the continuation of the Kaiser Wilhelm Society, is one of the most respected scientific research institutions in the world. Our research program is to provide the Society with additional resources to hire and train scientists and conduct fundamental research, based on the scientists' own interests.

@applied
title: Fund applied research in economically useful technologies.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; science += 1; applied_research += 1; economic_growth += 0.5 if economic_growth <= 8 and applied_research <= 1; economic_growth += 1 if applied_research > 1; white_collar_workers_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 1*(1-dissent); fdp_relation += 5*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress -= 1 if capital_strike_progress > 1; science_funding += 1

Our research program focuses on collaborating with industry to develop useful technologies, creating new research institutions for applied science. This collaboration is focused on economic growth and development.

@medical
title: Fund biomedical research at the hospitals and medical schools.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; science += 1; medical_research += 1; economic_growth += 0.4 if economic_growth <= 8; white_collar_workers_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 1*(1-dissent); fdp_relation += 5*(1-dissent); science_funding += 1

Our research program focuses on medical research to improve the treatment of diseases and public health. [? if change_sex: Some of our medical advancements include new methods for sex change surgery and hormone therapy for transsexual individuals. ?]

@cut_funding
title: Cut science funding.
subtitle: +1 budget
choose-if: science_funding >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have not funded science.
on-arrival: budget += 1; science -= 1; science_funding -= 1; applied_research -= 0.33; mpg_research -= 0.33; medical_research -= 0.33; economic_growth -= 0.5; new_middle_spd -= 3; workers_spd -= 1.5; fdp_relation -= 5

We have cut funding for science. This has a negative effect on our economic growth, and unemployed scientists are less likely to support the SPD.

@structure
title: Change the structure and funding of education.

Education in Germany is still divided among class lines. It is a part of our platform to ensure equal opportunities and make it easier for working class children to go to university.

- @public_hs
- @school_boards
- @ed_menu: Do not change school funding or organization.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@public_hs
title: Increase educational opportunities for the working class by funding public high schools.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; public_hs += 1; workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.5; economic_growth += 0.2; pro_republic += 4*(1-dissent);
max-visits: 3

# this makes the bureaucracy more proletarian
We have funded more public secondary schools so that proletarian children may receive the same education as middle and upper-class children, and can be prepared for universities.


@school_boards
title: Create elected school boards to give local areas more control over education.
on-arrival: school_boards += 1; workers_spd += 1*(1-dissent); white_collar_workers_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent); self_employed_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.2;
view-if: school_boards = 0

We have created local elected school boards, and delegated some of the decision-making for local schools to them.


@curriculum
title: Change the educational curriculum.
choose-if: curriculum_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if curriculum_timer > 0 : It is too early to change the curriculum again. ?]

Many socialists believe that education in Germany is not fit for the modern era. Much of the educational system is still outdated. Nevertheless, there have been strides in bringing working-class children into higher tier schools.

What should be the major focus of our new curriculum?

- @dem_major
- @science_major
- @human_major
- @vocational_major
- @trad_major
- @ed_menu: Do not change the curriculum now.
- @cancel_advisor_action

# note: education_science is a variable that affects how much education affects economic growth.

@dem_major
title: Democratic curriculum
subtitle: Critical thinking, democratic citizenship, and collaboration
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "democratic"; pro_republic += 5*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent); democratization += 1; cdu_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; pacifism += 1; education_science += 0.3
go-to: curriculum_minor

We should teach students how to be citizens of a democratic republic, by teaching them to critically evaluate politics and current events, to exercise their rights and to respect the rights of other citizens. Traditionalists of all stripes are critical of this curriculum.

@science_major
title: Scientific curriculum
subtitle: Modern science, mathematics, and technical skills
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "scientific"; education_science += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; cdu_relation -= 5; white_collar_workers_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 1*(1-dissent)
go-to: curriculum_minor

Our educational system should reflect the modern age, and we should teach science and rational thinking. Religious conservatives tend to react negatively against this. 

@human_major
title: Humanist curriculum
subtitle: Arts, literature, history, and philosophy
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "humanist"; white_collar_workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.2
go-to: curriculum_minor

Our educational curriculum should be focused on the humanities, including arts, literature, history, and philosophy. Some criticize this curriculum as focusing too much on "useless" subjects, while others worry that the arts establishment is too closely tied to romantic nationalism.

@vocational_major
title: Vocational curriculum
subtitle: Useful technical skills for future careers
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "vocational"; workers_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 2*(1-dissent); white_collar_workers_spd -= 1; education_science += 0.5
go-to: curriculum_minor

Education should be focused on providing a useful hands-on education, and teach the skills that will be most useful for students' future lives.


@trad_major
title: Traditional curriculum
subtitle: Classics, discipline, and nationalism
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "traditional"; cdu_relation += 5; self_employed_spd += 2*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 2*(1-dissent); pacifism -= 1 if pacifism > 0; pro_republic -= 5; education_science += 0.2
go-to: curriculum_minor

The traditional curriculum had a focus on ancient history and language (particularly Latin and Greek), as well as rigid discipline and some level of militarism.


@curriculum_minor

And what should be a secondary focus of the curriculum?

- @dem_minor
- @science_minor
- @human_minor
- @vocational_minor
- @trad_minor

@dem_minor
title: Democratic curriculum
subtitle: Critical thinking, democratic citizenship, and collaboration
view-if: major_curriculum != "democratic"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "democratic"; pro_republic += 3*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 1*(1-dissent); democratization += 1; cdu_relation -= 3;

We should teach students how to be citizens of a democratic republic, by teaching them to critically evaluate politics and current events, to exercise their rights and to respect the rights of other citizens. Traditionalists of all stripes are critical of this curriculum.

@science_minor
title: Scientific curriculum
subtitle: Modern science, mathematics, and technical skills
view-if: major_curriculum != "scientific"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "scientific"; education_science += 0.5; cdu_relation -= 3; white_collar_workers_spd += 1*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 1*(1-dissent)

Our educational system should reflect the modern age, and we should teach science and rational thinking. Religious conservatives tend to react negatively against this. 

@human_minor
title: Humanist curriculum
subtitle: Arts, literature, history, and philosophy
view-if: major_curriculum != "humanist"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "humanist"; white_collar_workers_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent)

Our educational curriculum should be focused on the humanities, including arts, literature, history, and philosophy. Some criticize this curriculum as focusing too much on "useless" subjects, while others worry that the arts establishment is too closely tied to romantic nationalism.

@vocational_minor
title: Vocational curriculum
subtitle: Useful technical skills for future careers
view-if: major_curriculum != "vocational"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "vocational"; education_science += 0.3; workers_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent)

Education should be focused on providing a useful hands-on education, and teach the skills that will be most useful for students' future lives.

@trad_minor
title: Traditional curriculum
subtitle: Classics, discipline, and nationalism
view-if: major_curriculum != "traditional"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "traditional"; cdu_relation += 3; self_employed_spd += 1*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 1*(1-dissent); pro_republic -= 3

The traditional curriculum had a focus on ancient history and language (particularly Latin and Greek), as well as rigid discipline.
